{
  // The SPA's type-check, and ONLY its type-check — `noEmit` is the point.
  //
  // WHY THIS FILE DID NOT EXIST UNTIL #201. Vite never needed it: Vite 8 hands
  // `.ts`/`.tsx` to oxc, which STRIPS types and never checks them, so the 27
  // TypeScript files under `src/` shipped unverified. `npm run test:types` is
  // the worker's tsconfig, and `npm run lint:undef` is globbed `{js,jsx}`
  // because espree cannot parse TypeScript — so against a missing import, which
  // is a runtime ReferenceError the bundler emits without complaint, these files
  // were covered by nothing but fourteen hard-coded hook names.
  //
  // STRICT IS THE SMALL OPTION HERE, WHICH IS NOT THE OBVIOUS WAY ROUND and is
  // why it is worth a note. Measured over exactly these files: fully loose
  // reports 15 errors, `noImplicitAny` alone 18, and strict 10. Loose mode reads
  // `data.features[idx] ?? {}` in `demo_day_app.tsx` as narrowing to the empty
  // type and reports seven property errors against a defensive fallback that is
  // already correct; under `strictNullChecks` the left side is known non-nullish,
  // the `??` narrows away, and all seven vanish. `allowJs` takes the last one —
  // `decks/spinout/deckData.js` is the only `.js` any of these files import, and
  // admitting it lets TS infer the shape instead of refusing the import. That is
  // 9 to fix, all nine fixed, and the whole check runs in about 1.4s.
  //
  // `checkJs` stays OFF on purpose: this types one import, it does not quietly
  // make the SPA's JavaScript a type-check target.
  //
  // `noUnusedLocals` (D164) is what closes the OTHER half of the gap this file
  // was created for. Eighteen CodeQL "unused variable" alerts landed at once,
  // seven of them in one `.tsx` file, and nothing in the repo could see them:
  // `check-unused-imports.mjs` only matches `const {` destructures, and
  // `eslint.config.mjs` is globbed `{js,jsx}`. This flag costs nothing — with
  // the dead declarations swept, `tsc` reports zero across all 27 files — and
  // it is the cheapest lever available, being one line on a check already
  // wired into `test:drift`.
  //
  // `noUnusedParameters` is deliberately NOT set: it adds 11 findings that are
  // all positional callback parameters, the same class `eslint.config.mjs`
  // excludes with `args: 'none'` and for the same reason.
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "lib": ["ES2022", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    "strict": true,
    "noUnusedLocals": true,
    "allowJs": true,
    "checkJs": false,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "forceConsistentCasingInFileNames": true,
    "noEmit": true
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts", "src/**/*.tsx"]
}
